# Resume fence — first-hop arming

`operator_message ~ ^resume \d+ ⇒`

1. **First ULG hop:** `continuity(op=resume, thread=T)`. On `user-vortex-code` it is **overflow**: `dispatch(tool="continuity", arguments='{"op":"resume","thread":"T"}')` (direct `continuity` ⇒ not found). ¬ `GetDynamicTools` / `tool_search` first — the hook nudges those bleed tools while `armed`, and never denies.
2. Pour is one `tape` call (or the inline bundle). `tape`, `get`, `cortex`, `rename_chat`, `retrieve`, and file reads stay undenied. An `rs_*` handle is `retrieve`d exactly once — it pops.
3. Cite ids from the returned `read_set.citable` when the bundle landed. A durable `agent_bus send` may carry the bundle's `fence_id`; pass `transcript_id` on `continuity(op=resume)` when the tab id is known (FIX-15).

The IDE hook is a first-hop nudge, ¬ a lock; `permission` is never `deny`. `sessionStart` drops the local marker so a Cursor restart unfences the tab.

## Bundle pickup — verbatim before paraphrase

Read the bundle top-down before any sketchboard, card, or prior-tab prose. A lower row does not outrank the tip; row 1.5 orients intent and does not override the tip's facts. Spoken reply is `operator-posture` Rule 3, starting at the aim — this block does not open it. Fence id and head sha join the receipts line. `open_line: null` is normal — never fill that gap from a sketchboard.

